{"chunk_id": "3f009d0566e4", "text": "This chapter launches Hanuman\u2019s legendary leap across the ocean in search of the abducted Sita. Expanding his body to colossal size on a mountain crowded with celestial beings, he vows to reach Lanka or bring Ravana back in chains. His leap shakes the earth and sends trees and flowers flying as he rockets into the sky like a meteor. The gods watch and aid him: the ocean raises the golden mountain Mainaka to offer him rest, recalling an ancient debt to the Wind-god, but Hanuman refuses to delay his mission. The serpent-mother Surasa tests him by demanding he enter her mouth; he outwits her by shrinking and escaping. Later the shadow\u2011seizing demoness Singhika attacks, and Hanuman slays her from within. The chapter celebrates courage, divine favor, and ingenuity as Hanuman\u2019s mythic journey toward Lanka begins.\nHanuman launches his immense leap across the ocean toward Lanka, overcoming tests from Mainaka, Surasa, and the demoness Simhika.\nThemes: heroic quest, divine assistance, tests of strength and wit, devotion to Rama, journey across the ocean", "vector": [0.02207311987876892, -0.017584120854735374, -0.0023988911416381598, -0.004259899724274874, -0.010033839382231236, 0.016548199579119682, -0.03585885837674141, -0.005959874950349331, -0.021475471556186676, -0.02913864329457283, 0.005588005296885967, 0.018208330497145653, 0.013154888525605202, 0.007185052614659071, 0.023719970136880875, -7.429091783706099e-05, 0.03293702378869057, -0.02948394976556301, 0.018699729815125465, -0.01499431487172842, -0.012530678883194923, -0.01826145499944687, -0.001409452292136848, 0.0206122025847435, -0.013825582340359688, 0.0017514396458864212, 0.024875422939658165, -0.037001028656959534, 0.020373143255710602, -0.009974074549973011, -0.003126029158011079, -0.016920069232583046, -0.005800502374768257, -0.0076631708070635796, -0.016455231234431267, 0.007264738902449608, -0.006185653153806925, -0.015910707414150238, 0.008420190773904